**Expanding Exclusions Feature**

I'm currently focused on the "Negative Constraints" feature within the LyricsTab. Right now, I have a text input and a list of preset excluded keywords. The goal is to extend this section's functionality. My plan is to introduce a UI for easier management of these exclusions. I envision this UI as separate from the simple text input, and I am exploring the best way to accomplish this.


**Defining Custom Presets**

I'm now thinking about how to best implement the custom preset functionality within LyricsTab. I plan to add state for `customPresets` and load them from `localStorage` upon mounting. I will then add a "Save as Preset" button next to the text input. The "Save as Preset" will save user-defined keywords to the `customPresets` array. I also plan to add a UI element to delete the created presets.


**Designing the Preset UI**

I'm now zeroing in on the UI for custom keyword presets. I plan to put a "Save Preset" button beside the "Add" button in the input field. Clicking "Save Preset" will add the input to `customPresets` and save it to `localStorage`. I'll show `customPresets` alongside the default presets and add a delete button (an 'x') next to each custom preset to enable easy removal from the list.


**Finalizing Preset Interaction**

I'm now thinking specifically about how the user will interact with the presets. I've decided custom presets will have a visual indicator or a remove button on the preset chip. Clicking a preset should toggle it in the excluded list, as before. I have also decided to keep custom presets visually distinct or grouped from the existing presets. For the code, I'll add a function `handleAddCustomPreset`, which takes a keyword, adds it to `customPresets` (if unique), and saves to `localStorage`. I'll import `useEffect` and set up the `customPresets` state in `LyricsTab.tsx`.


